course: dictionary
lesson: 529
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the context: the words and sentences around it. «Astronomers measure the solar system in astronomical units, where 1 AU is Earth's average distance from the Sun, about 150 million km.» Here the sentence is about planets and the Sun, so astronomical means to do with astronomy, the science of stars, planets and space.
explain: People also use astronomical in everyday talk, and then it means something different. «The tickets cost astronomical prices, so we stayed at home.» Nobody is looking at stars here. The price is extremely large, so astronomical means very, very expensive.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «The tickets cost extremely large prices, so we stayed at home» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. If a sentence is about space, check the science meaning instead. If it is about money or numbers, the informal meaning is probably right.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is called a multiple-meaning word. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: «Astronomical» means to do with astronomy, the science of stars, planets and space.
fact: Informally, «astronomical» means extremely large, especially about prices or numbers.
fact: An astronomical unit is the distance from Earth to the Sun, about 150 million kilometres.
fact: «Astronomically» is the adverb form, as in «astronomically expensive».
exercise: «Astronomers measure the solar system in astronomical units.» In this sentence, astronomical means | *About space and stars | Very quiet | Very cheap | Very soft
exercise: «The tickets cost astronomical prices, so we stayed at home.» What does astronomical mean here? | To do with stars and planets | Very small | Easy to pay for | *Extremely large, very expensive
exercise: Which sentence uses astronomical with the science meaning? | Her astronomical sandwich was huge and cheap | The astronomical sum on the bill made Dad gasp | *A telescope helps astronomers study distant planets | The astronomical queue was very short
test: An astronomical unit is about how far? | *150 million km | 150 metres | 1 million km | 15 km
test: Which word is the adverb form of astronomical? | astronomer | *astronomically | astronomy | astronomic
exam: In maths, «astronomical numbers» means | *Huge numbers | Numbers written in words | Tiny numbers | Numbers about stars
